From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 16:59:43 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: cfg80211: add DFS test files to debugfs

DFS tests wait for a 60 s CAC, a 10 min weather radar CAC or a 30 min
non-occupancy period, and a radar detection rate test fires many
radar bursts at an AP that holds its channel. Neither the DFS state
of a channel nor the number of reported radar events is visible
without netlink tools.

Each wiphy gets a debugfs file in fixed columns for awk and grep. It
shows the radar event count and the last event. It lists the 5 GHz
links and the background chain by interface name, with their CAC
timers. It lists each radar channel with its DFS state, running
timer, radar counts per chain and covering chain. Root-only files
zero the counters, end a running CAC, end every non-occupancy period,
or return available channels to usable. They bypass regulatory timers
and are for tests only. An event counts on each radar sub-channel of
its chandef under a spinlock, because the background chain reports
from the driver without the wiphy lock. A station link gets its
channel from the driver, because cfg80211 keeps no chandef for it. An
AP link with a chandef but no beacon and no CAC shows as idle,
because the chandef stays after an aborted CAC. A skipped CAC sends
one CAC finished event, the same as a CAC that runs to its end. The
handlers run under the wiphy lock, because they walk the interface
list, change the DFS state and call the driver.

Based-on-patch-by: StanleyYP Wang <StanleyYP.Wang@mediatek.com>
Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
